    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-053: Honor viewport units in max-width / max-height clamps**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (4 lines removed + 3 tests) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nCloses one more sticky-sidebar prerequisite: `max-width: 100vw`, `max-height: 100vh`, and `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)` now clamp for the first time.\n\n## The discovery\n\n`layout.cpp:1734-1786` already has **all four clamps** (min-width, max-width, min-height, max-height) from ADR-039's box model. Three work correctly. Two paths skip vw/vh — **that guard is stale**:\n\n| Property | vw/vh guard? | % guard? | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `min-width` | No | No | Works |\n| `max-width` | **Skips vw/vh** | No | Guard stale |\n| `min-height` | No | Only `%` | Works |\n| `max-height` | **Skips vw/vh** | Also `%` | vw/vh guard stale |\n\n## Why the guard was added (ADR-037 era)\n\nAt ADR-037 time, `parse_length(\"100vw\")` returned 0. A `max-width: 100vw` that resolved to 0 would trigger `if (0 < content_w) content_w = 0` and **collapse the element**. ADR-037 skipped vw/vh entirely — the correct defensive choice at the time.\n\n## What changed since\n\n- **ADR-051** added vw/vh/vmin/vmax to `parse_length` (and `parse_operand`)\n- **ADR-052** made `ctx.viewport_height` nonzero in production\n\nThe bug the guard protected against is fixed. The guard is stale.\n\n## Why removal is safe (the `> 0.0f` safety net)\n\nThe clamp code already contains:\n\n```cpp\nif (max_w > 0.0f && max_w < content_w) content_w = max_w;\nif (max_h > 0.0f && max_h < (cursor_y - content_y)) {\n    cursor_y = content_y + max_h;\n}\n```\n\nBoth gate on `> 0.0f`. If `parse_length` returns 0 (initial render, viewport_w = 0 before GTK allocation), the clamp is skipped — **no collapse**. The safety net ADR-037 needed is already in the code; it just wasn't trusted at the time.\n\n## What is NOT being removed\n\n- **`%` guard on max-height** — `parent_content_height` threading is separate; `%` heights resolve to viewport **width** today, which is catastrophic\n- **`> 0.0f` safety checks** — the initial-render safety net\n\n## What is being removed (4 lines)\n\n```\nxw->find(\"vw\") == std::string::npos &&\nxw->find(\"vh\") == std::string::npos &&\nxh->find(\"vh\") == std::string::npos &&\nxh->find(\"vw\") == std::string::npos &&\n```\n\nPlus comment updates (ADR-037/ADR-039 rationale now cites ADR-053).\n\n## Three new tests (644 → 647)\n\n```\n1. width: 5000px; max-width: 100vw  @ viewport_w=1024  → box.width = 1024\n2. height: 5000px; max-height: 100vh @ viewport_h=678 → box.height = 678\n3. height: 5000px; max-height: calc(100vh - 48px) @ 678 → box.height = 630\n```\n\n**These are ADR-053's verified delta.** Zero tests today exercise layout-level max/min clamps — the guard has never been tested.\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Zero visible PNG delta.** `.vector-sticky-pinned-container` is `h=0` from ancestor culling; the clamp fires but the element has nothing to clamp. Same category as ADR-047/048: correct infrastructure shipped before its consumer.\n\n**What changes semantically**: `max-width: 100vw` now yields `content_w = viewport_w`; `max-height: calc(100vh - 48px)` now yields `cursor_y = content_y + (viewport_h - 48)`. Both correct for the first time.\n\n## Prerequisite chain\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `@supports (display: grid)` gate | ✅ ADR-050 |\n| `calc(100vh - 48px)` parses | ✅ ADR-051 |\n| `viewport_h` in production | ✅ ADR-052 |\n| **Layout reads `max-height`** | ✅ **ADR-053 (this ADR)** |\n| Ancestor culling | ❌ pending (separate) |\n| `position: sticky` scroll-Y | ❌ pending (separate) |\n\n## Verification\n\n**Unit tests (primary):** 3 new tests prove clamps fire.\n\n**Log verification (secondary):** `HONEYBEE_LOG=layout` unchanged; no crash; 647/2471 pass.\n\n**PNG verification (honest zero):** before/after screenshots identical.\n\nRefs #239\n",
